{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Make Animal Harm Warnings Mandatory in All Film and Television",
        "additional_details": "These warnings should clearly inform viewers when a programme contains scenes of animal injury, suffering, abuse or death, regardless of whether the events are fictional, simulated or real.\r\n\r\nMany viewers find animal suffering particularly distressing and may wish to avoid such scenes. Currently, people often have to search online for spoilers or consult third-party websites to find out whether an animal is harmed.\r\n\r\nA consistent, easily accessible warning system would allow viewers to make informed choices before watching, without revealing unnecessary plot details.\r\n\r\nWe believe audiences should have the right to know when animal suffering features in the entertainment they choose to watch.",
        "background": "We call on the UK Government to introduce mandatory animal-content warnings across films and television programmes, including streaming services.",
